<urn:atm:triage:finding/INTEGRATE-PAI3133-CIRED-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "INTEGRATE-PAI3133-CIRED-001" ;
  triage:title "integrate/phase-ai-31-33 base branch carries two pre-existing fmt/clippy violations that turn every open PR's merge-preview CI red" ;
  triage:description "PR #691 (AI.37) shows CI-red on Format check + Just lint (all 3 platforms) despite: (a) AI37's own diff touching neither flagged file (git diff origin/integrate/phase-ai-31-33...feature/pAI-s37-hermes-recovery-summary is empty for both paths), (b) local cargo fmt --check/clippy/just lint all clean inside the AI37 worktree, and (c) all 4 dispatched AI37-QA-2 reviewers independently reporting PASS. Root-caused by fetching GitHub's actual synthetic merge-preview commit (refs/pull/691/merge) and running rustfmt/clippy directly against it: two violations exist on integrate/phase-ai-31-33 itself, pre-dating AI.37's branch point, and surface only when the pull_request-triggered CI job's default actions/checkout@v4 (no explicit ref:) checks out the merge-preview commit instead of the raw PR head. (1) crates/atm-architecture/tests/graft_receiver_ownership_boundary.rs:29-34 fails `cargo fmt --check` (single-line assert_eq! chain that rustfmt wants split to multi-line) — this is already fixed on fix/ai36-qa-repair @ bca831f7 (PR #692, currently green on all 8 CI legs) and will self-resolve once #692 merges into integrate/phase-ai-31-33; it is NOT yet fixed on integrate/phase-ai-31-33 itself. (2) crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs:1661 fails clippy::bool_assert_comparison (`assert_eq!(registry.try_register(MAX_PEER_HTTP_CONNECTIONS).is_none(), true, ...)`) — present directly on integrate/phase-ai-31-33 (confirmed via git show origin/integrate/phase-ai-31-33:crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs), unrelated to any file AI.37 or AI.36 touched; requires its own dedicated one-line fix (assert!(...) or assert_eq!(..., true) -> assert!(...)) directly on integrate/phase-ai-31-33." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci_gap" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "cross_branch" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:blockingCurrentMerge true ;
  triage:note "Remediation: (1) merge PR #692 (fix/ai36-qa-repair @ bca831f7 or later) into integrate/phase-ai-31-33 to pick up the already-fixed graft_receiver_ownership_boundary.rs formatting; (2) separately fix the pre-existing clippy::bool_assert_comparison at crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs:1661 directly on integrate/phase-ai-31-33 (assert!(registry.try_register(MAX_PEER_HTTP_CONNECTIONS).is_none(), ...) in place of assert_eq!(..., true)). Blocks CI-green merge readiness for every open PR targeting integrate/phase-ai-31-33 (confirmed affecting PR #691; PR #692 itself is unaffected because its own branch already carries fix (1), and its assert_eq! literal-bool at the same base-branch location does not get promoted to a hard clippy error in that run — not yet root-caused, but immaterial since #692 is already green). Not attributable to AI.37's or AI.36's own diffs." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI37-QA-2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-29T09:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-29T09:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/INTEGRATE-PAI3133-CIRED-001/fmt-graft-boundary> ,
    <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/INTEGRATE-PAI3133-CIRED-001/clippy-https-transport> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/phase-AI/integrate-phase-ai-31-33> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "integrate/phase-ai-31-33" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

